  "llm_analysis": {
    "hotspots": "Large Language Models (LLMs) and Foundation Models; Multimodal Video Understanding & Temporal Reasoning; Embodied AI / Robotics (World Models, Trajectory Optimization); Model Evaluation, Auditing & Quality Assurance; Scaling Laws & Training Efficiency.",
    "trends": "Shift from static language modeling to dynamic multimodal (video) and temporal reasoning; Deep integration of LLMs into Robotics/Control via World Models and trajectory prediction; Maturation of evaluation methodologies focusing on auditability, robustness, and 'non-fixed' target analysis; Emphasis on data quality and specific information curation over raw scale; Rise of agentic workflows and multi-agent systems in SE and SI contexts.",
    "future_directions": "Development of Generalist World Models unifying perception, reasoning, and action; Self-evolving / Self-correcting models with formal verification guarantees; Efficient architectures beyond standard Transformers (e.g., state-space, non-attention mechanisms); Sim-to-Real transfer and lifelong learning for robotic trajectories; Standardized, dynamic benchmarking ecosystems for continuous audit and safety alignment.",
    "analysis_summary": "The current landscape reflects a consolidation phase where Foundation Models act as universal backbones across CV, RO, CL, and LG. Research priority has pivoted from pure scaling to capability grounding—specifically temporal/video understanding and physical interaction (trajectories/world models). The prominence of 'audit', 'quality', 'evaluation', and 'fixed/non-fixed target analysis' signals a community-wide push toward reliability, safety, and scientific rigor, moving beyond leaderboard chasing toward deployable, trustworthy AI systems."
